==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|grass|t=informer}}<ref>''The New Partridge Dictionary of Slang'' {{ISBN|0415259371}}</ref> + {{m|en|up}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-grass up.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|UK|slang}} To [[betray]] by [[informant|informing on]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Angela Devlin; Bob Turney|title=Going Straight: After Crime and Punishment|isbn=187287066X
|passage=My sister '''grassed''' me '''up''' to the caretaker! She thought she was doing me a favour — by '''grassing''' me '''up''' she was sure he'd let me off.}}

